{"term":"database","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:cd22fc542c8c930f97","definition":"A collection of (usually) organized information in a regular structure, usually but not necessarily in a machine-readable format accessible by a computer.","example":"I have a database of all my contacts in my personal organizer.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["data set","dataset","databank"],"antonyms":["nondatabase"],"collocations":[],"usage":"broadly","register":"broadly","wordFamily":["database administrator","database analyst","database dump","database engine","database-first","database key","databaselike","database management system","database model","database publishing","database transaction","hyperbase","tablebase","termbase","textbase"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/database#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:5e3fc1b3210e34915c","definition":"A set of tables and other objects (queries, reports, forms) in the form of a structured data set.","example":"The \"books\" database will have three tables, and the \"customers\" database will have two tables.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["DB","database management system"],"antonyms":["nondatabase"],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["database administrator","database analyst","database dump","database engine","database-first","database key","databaselike","database management system","database model","database publishing","database transaction","hyperbase","tablebase","termbase","textbase"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/database#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8511157131fe970f6d","definition":"A software program (application) for storing, retrieving and manipulating such a structured data set.","example":"Which database do you use: MySQL or Oracle?","pos":"noun","synonyms":["DB","databas